==Battleground==
*1 [[Bore]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Bakoo]] spawns as the boss.
**2 [[Bore]]s spawn, delay 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
**20 [[Wall Doge]]s spawn, delay 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
**1 [[Kang Roo]] spawns.

==Strategy==
An easy strategy is to stall the first Bore with [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]] and build up your funds for the actual fight. Once the desired amount is acquired, kill off the first Bore and proceed to the enemy base. Continue the process with the second Bore by luring him to your base, and use [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance Cats]] to chip away Bakoo's health. [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave attackers]] such as [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cat]] or [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]] are useful as well, but are still frozen by Bakoo.

While the boss's standing range is very low (180), her Long Distance hits extremely far away (from 50 to 1,800), and it still allows her to hide behind the pair of Bores that guard her. As such, you either kill the frontline quickly and rush the boss, or use Long Distance and waves to kill the boss. Additionally, while she does have a blind spot, entering it without clipping is practically impossible.

Keep in mind that, if a short-ranged unit attacks the enemy base when the boss wave happens, Bakoo will attack when she spawns, freezing and possibly killing every unit in her enormous range. To prevent this, the [[Cat Cannon]] must be fired before the boss wave is triggered, knocking her back and interrupting her attack. If fired too soon or too late, the player will be placed at a severe disadvantage that they likely won't recover from. A well-timed [[Ototo Corps|Breakerblast]] can help here, as it is easier to time than the normal Cat Cannon. Additionally, the Breakerblast is useful throughout the middle of the fight as well assuming that she can be put in range due to the ease of timing.

[[Ototo Corps#Slow Beam|Slow Beam]], [[Ototo Corps#Thunderbolt|Thunderbolt]], and [[Ototo Corps#Holy Blast|Holy Blast]] will not work for this strategy.

[[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cats]] and [[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rare Cats]] who are immune to Freeze or can deal with Bores from a distance can greatly increase your odds, with good examples being [[Bunny & Canard (Uber Rare Cat)|Bunny & Canard]], [[Baby Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Cats in the Cradle]], [[Akuma (Legend Rare Cat)|Akuma]], and [[Thundia (Uber Rare Cat)|Thundia]]. [[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST]] and [[UBERFEST (Gacha Event)|UBERFEST]] exclusives are even more effective here.

